---
description: Switchboard project rules (always on)
alwaysApply: true
---
- Read docs/PLAN.md §17 and docs/DESIGN.md before any task.
- Goal: win Agent Memory and Coordination (second: Connected Data) with a product where FalkorDB does the real work (claims checked against a parsed code dependency graph, decisions and history in the same graph), plus a polished UI, a landing page with real benchmark numbers, and a demo that can't fail. Check every change against this goal (PLAN §17.8).
- Touch only the files your brief lists. Branch hack/<id>; parallel tasks in their own git worktree (PLAN §17.4). Never commit to main directly.
- FalkorDB is the only store. Cypher lives in packages/core/src/queries/*.ts with tests against a real FalkorDB.
- Claim a file before editing it (`claim` or `switchboard claim`). On CONFLICT, stop. `SWITCHBOARD_OFF=1` disables the editor hooks.
- No secrets in git. No new dependency without saying why.
- Model policy: main chat Claude Opus 5.5; subagents and small tasks Grok 4.7; big tasks Opus 5.5.
- End with: summary, `git diff --stat main`, test output and a DEVLOG entry.
